AND YOU'RE STILL NOT STOPPING.

479
00:17:05,763 --> 00:17:07,465
YOU GO--YOU'RE MAKING IT WORSE.

480
00:17:07,465 --> 00:17:10,167
FOR ME TO FOCUS
IN THIS COMPETITION...

481
00:17:10,167 --> 00:17:12,470
YES, I NEED JOHN TO BACK OFF
A LITTLE BIT.

482
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:14,238
WE WILL HAVE
ANY DEEP CONVERSATIONS

483
00:17:14,238 --> 00:17:15,306
WHEN I GET HOME FROM...

484
00:17:15,306 --> 00:17:16,440
- First of all...
- AND I'M SERIOUS.

485
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,708
First of all
first of all...

486
00:17:17,708 --> 00:17:18,709
(hangs up phone)

487
00:17:18,709 --> 00:17:22,179
♪♪♪

488
00:17:27,484 --> 00:17:29,252
♪♪♪

489
00:17:29,252 --> 00:17:32,021
I THINK I DID THE WORST
IN THE CHALLENGE TODAY.

490
00:17:32,021 --> 00:17:34,091
I FEEL THAT THIS WEEK
IT'S REALLY IMPORTANT FOR ME

491
00:17:34,091 --> 00:17:36,660
TO STEP IT UP AND DO WELL,
JUST BECAUSE I HAVEN'T BEEN

492
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,862
DOING WELL IN THE PAST.

493
00:17:37,862 --> 00:17:40,531
I HAVE TO KICK ASS IN MY PHOTO
SHOOT TOMORROW.

494
00:17:41,966 --> 00:17:43,834
MM-HMM.

495
00:17:43,834 --> 00:17:45,770
Y'ALL, WE GOT TYRA MAIL!

496
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:48,305
"AT 10 YEARS OLD, YOU SAID,
'WHEN I GROW UP,

497
00:17:48,305 --> 00:17:49,640
I WANNA BE A MODEL.'

498
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,476
I HOPE YOU'RE NOT STILL
SAYING THAT WHEN YOU'RE MY AGE.

499
00:17:52,476 --> 00:17:53,544
TYRA."

500
00:17:53,544 --> 00:17:55,579
- WHAT?
- WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

501
00:17:55,579 --> 00:17:58,082
MAYBE WE'LL ALL BE, LIKE,
LITTLE KIDS RUNNING AROUND.

502
00:17:58,082 --> 00:17:59,450
(laughing)

503
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:00,584
WE'RE JUST TRYING TO COME UP
WITH ALL THESE SCENARIOS,

504
00:18:00,584 --> 00:18:01,786
AND USUALLY,
THEY'RE WRONG ANYWAYS.

505
00:18:01,786 --> 00:18:03,020
I'M LIKE, "THERE'S NO POINT
IN TRYING

506
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,355
TO COME UP WITH ANYTHING."

507
00:18:05,222 --> 00:18:10,194
♪♪♪

508
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,601
(cheering)

509
00:18:17,601 --> 00:18:18,836
OH!

510
00:18:18,836 --> 00:18:21,005
(cheering)

511
00:18:21,005 --> 00:18:22,840
HI!

512
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:23,941
HOW ARE Y'ALL?

513
00:18:23,941 --> 00:18:25,209
HOW ARE YOU DOING?

514
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:26,811
(all) GOOD.
- WELCOME!

515
00:18:26,811 --> 00:18:30,047
YOU'RE AT MY SHOW,
AND THIS IS MY DRESSING ROOM.

516
00:18:30,047 --> 00:18:33,317
WHEN I WAS 15, 16 YEARS OLD,
I WANTED TO BE A MODEL,

517
00:18:33,317 --> 00:18:35,953
AND I REALLY DEDICATED MYSELF
TO BEING A MODEL.

518
00:18:35,953 --> 00:18:38,789
BUT AT THE BACK OF MY MIND,
I ALWAYS KNEW THAT

519
00:18:38,789 --> 00:18:40,391
IT WAS A TEMPORARY CAREER.

520
00:18:40,391 --> 00:18:42,760
WHAT I WANNA DO TODAY
IS I WANNA TALK TO ALL OF YOU

521
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:46,764
ABOUT YOUR FUTURE GOALS,
BECAUSE I WANT TO HELP RAISE

522
00:18:46,764 --> 00:18:50,100
VERY STRONG WOMEN AS WELL,
NOT JUST MODELS.

523
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,268
OKAY?

524
00:18:51,268 --> 00:18:53,838
SO, DANIELLE,
WHAT ARE YOUR FUTURE GOALS?

525
00:18:53,838 --> 00:18:55,472
WHEN I WAS A LITTLE GIRL,
I WANTED TO BE A SINGER.

526
00:18:55,472 --> 00:18:56,807
LIKE, THAT IS WHAT
I WANTED TO DO.

527
00:18:56,807 --> 00:18:57,908
BUT I DO NOT HAVE A VOICE.

528
00:18:57,908 --> 00:18:59,176
ALL RIGHT, FURONDA,
WHAT ABOUT YOU?

529
00:18:59,176 --> 00:19:02,446
I WANNA BE AN ATTORNEY,
AND I WANNA DO MOSTLY

530
00:19:02,446 --> 00:19:03,747
HUMAN RIGHTS LAW.

531
00:19:03,747 --> 00:19:05,316
I WANTED
TO GO INTO CRIMINAL JUSTICE.

532
00:19:05,316 --> 00:19:06,717
- CRIMINAL JUSTICE?
- YEAH.

533
00:19:06,717 --> 00:19:09,119
NO MATTER WHAT, I WANNA STAY
IN THE FASHION INDUSTRY,

534
00:19:09,119 --> 00:19:11,088
UM, WHETHER IT'S EVEN
HAIR AND MAKEUP.

535
00:19:11,088 --> 00:19:13,023
I WAS ACTUALLY THINKING ABOUT
GOING TO DESIGN SCHOOL

536
00:19:13,023 --> 00:19:14,091
FOR A WHILE.

537
00:19:14,091 --> 00:19:15,326
- FOR FASHION DESIGN?
- YEAH.

538
00:19:15,326 --> 00:19:17,494
I THINK IT, UH,
A REALLY IMPORTANT JOB

539
00:19:17,494 --> 00:19:19,263
IS, UM, BEING A MOTHER.

540
00:19:19,263 --> 00:19:21,999
I'VE WANTED CHILDREN
FOR SO LONG,

541
00:19:21,999 --> 00:19:24,468
BUT I FEEL LIKE I HAVE TO BE
AT A PLACE IN MY LIFE

542
00:19:24,468 --> 00:19:26,303
WHERE I'M MORE SETTLED.

543
00:19:26,303 --> 00:19:27,805
I LOVE CHILDREN,
AND I WANNA BE

544
00:19:27,805 --> 00:19:28,839
A KINDERGARTEN TEACHER.

545
00:19:28,839 --> 00:19:29,874
A KINDERGARTEN TEACHER?

546
00:19:29,874 --> 00:19:31,141
YES, 'CAUSE I LOVE KIDS.

547
00:19:31,141 --> 00:19:34,245
IT'S JUST SO RANDOM
TO HEAR JADE SAY SHE WANTS TO BE

548
00:19:34,245 --> 00:19:35,379
A KINDERGARTEN TEACHER.

549
00:19:35,379 --> 00:19:37,314
IF NEED BE,
I WOULD HOMESCHOOL MY CHILD

550
00:19:37,314 --> 00:19:39,183
BEFORE THEY WENT
TO JADE'S CLASS, MM-MM.

551
00:19:39,183 --> 00:19:41,685
I COULD SEE MYSELF, UM,
BEING A PROSECUTOR.

552
00:19:41,685 --> 00:19:43,020
I HAVE A DEGREE IN CHEMISTRY.

553
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:45,456
I SEE MYSELF
TRYING TO DO DRUG RESEARCH

554
00:19:45,456 --> 00:19:46,523
IN AFRICA.

555
00:19:46,523 --> 00:19:48,092
GOOD. WHAT ABOUT YOU, BROOKE?

556
00:19:48,092 --> 00:19:50,361
I WANT TO BE
A NURSE NECESSITIST.

557
00:19:50,361 --> 00:19:51,729
YOU MEAN, "ANESTHETIST"?

558
00:19:51,729 --> 00:19:52,863
YEAH. (chuckles)

559
00:19:52,863 --> 00:19:54,932
SO YOU WANT
TO PUT PEOPLE UNDER?

560
00:19:54,932 --> 00:19:56,066
BASICALLY.

561
00:19:56,066 --> 00:19:58,102
IT'S NOT SO MUCH
THAT TYRA MAKES ME NERVOUS.

562
00:19:58,102 --> 00:20:01,505
I JUST BECOME REALLY NERVOUS
THAT SHE MAY NOT LIKE ME.

563
00:20:01,505 --> 00:20:03,841
AND BECAUSE IT IS A COMPETITION,
I FEEL THAT EVERYTHING WE DO

564
00:20:03,841 --> 00:20:05,109
IS BEING JUDGED.

565
00:20:05,109 --> 00:20:08,145
WHEN I WAS... I THINK
I WAS 18 OR 19 YEARS OLD,

566
00:20:08,145 --> 00:20:10,247
I DID AN INTERVIEW
IN MILAN, ITALY,

567
00:20:10,247 --> 00:20:11,649
AND I WAS ALL YOUNG AND BUBBLY,

568
00:20:11,649 --> 00:20:13,083
LIKE, "I'M JUST HAPPY
TO DO AN INTERVIEW!"

569
00:20:13,083 --> 00:20:14,618
AND THEY WERE LIKE, "SO, TYRA,
WHAT ARE YOU GONNA BE DOING

570
00:20:14,618 --> 00:20:15,686
AFTER MODELING?"

571
00:20:15,686 --> 00:20:17,087
AND I'M LIKE,
"WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

572
00:20:17,087 --> 00:20:19,823
WHEN I'M 23 OR 24 YEARS OLD
I'M-A RETIRE FROM MODELING,

573
00:20:19,823 --> 00:20:21,759
AND I'M-A HAVE
MY OWN TALK SHOW."

574
00:20:21,759 --> 00:20:24,862
SO I DID MAKE
THIS TALK SHOW DREAM COME TRUE,

575
00:20:24,862 --> 00:20:26,931
AND IT'S BECAUSE
I ALWAYS HAD MY MIND ON THAT.

576
00:20:26,931 --> 00:20:28,999
WELL, I JUST FINISHED A SHOW,
AND NOW I GOTTA

577
00:20:28,999 --> 00:20:31,702
GO DO ANOTHER SHOW,
BUT I WANTED TO THANK Y'ALL

578
00:20:31,702 --> 00:20:33,137
FOR COMING.
(all) THANK YOU.

579
00:20:33,137 --> 00:20:35,205
AND SEEING, YOU KNOW,
MY--MY OTHER JOB.

580
00:20:35,205 --> 00:20:37,341
SO I'LL SEE YOU SOON!

581
00:20:37,341 --> 00:20:39,710
(all) BYE.
- (singsongy) BYE!

582
00:20:39,710 --> 00:20:43,814
♪♪♪

583
00:20:46,483 --> 00:20:48,452
SO YOU GUYS
JUST MET WITH TYRA, RIGHT?

584
00:20:48,452 --> 00:20:49,620
(all) YES.

585
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,256
TODAY YOU GIRLS
ARE ACTUALLY GOING TO ACT OUT

